  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency response for Returnees in Kabul, Balkh, Kunduz, Sarepul and Jawzjan Provinces</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will meet the immediate needs of returnees (from Pakistan and Iran) with a hybrid of inkind food/ hygiene kits, water trucking services, and multipurpose cash for 6 months, with targeted trainings. Vulnerable members of the host community will have the opportunity to participate in cash for work, or receive unconditional cash if they have no one able to work. Fresh food vouchers with growth monitoring screening to improve the nutrition of families of children in treatment for SAM and MAM.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed intervention aims to provide emergency support in the key areas of return and this way improve well-being and ensure safe and dignified returns of participants.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Total Participants: 95270.</narrative>
  </description>
